Subject: [PATCH] xilinx: pack shared carry S sources the same way whatever else is in the netlist

When a LUT drives the S inputs of several carry chains, the first chain
packed takes it into its carry site and the others get a copy
("<lut>$S_DUP<n>").  Both the choice and the copy's number depended on
the whole netlist: the chains were taken in cell-table order, which
erasing and creating cells reshuffles, and <n> came from the global
counter.  In a partial-reconfiguration flow the same static logic is
packed again with another module, and -o preplaced / -o prerouted find
its cells and nets by name, so a module with carry chains of its own
made the static logic pack differently (a sink path wire reserved for
both the LUT's net and its copy's).  Number the copies per source, and
with pblocks take the chains in name order.  Without pblocks the order
is unchanged; the copies' names are the only difference there.

Base: nextpnr-pblock-lutff.patch.  Not committed, not posted.
